# Seamline code owners.
#
# Every path here gets a required review from the listed owner. GitHub matches
# the LAST matching pattern, so the most specific rules go at the bottom.
#
# Owner: @zylv3r, the organisation owner. A CODEOWNERS entry pointing at a team
# that does not exist silently matches nobody, which produces a repository that
# looks reviewed and is not; the seamline-maintainers team does not exist, so a
# single real account is named instead. Move these entries back to a team the
# moment one exists with at least two members.

*                               @zylv3r

# The shared contract. Every package compiles against it, so a change here is a
# change to all of them at once.
/packages/ontology/             @zylv3r
/ontology/                      @zylv3r

# Identity, merge, lifecycle, and the store decorator that makes the redactor
# the sole writer to the store; a defect here is a disclosure, not a bug.
/packages/core/                 @zylv3r

# The redactor, the untrusted-text delimiting and the public injection corpus
# that tests them. A defect here is a disclosure or an injection, not a bug.
/packages/security/             @zylv3r

